Taken from crackdown-recomp (Unowa001) origin/main patches/sdk/0027-d3d12-present-latency-wait.patch (commit 66916ff): the swap chain is created with DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_FLAG_FRAME_LATENCY_WAITABLE_OBJECT (maximum latency 2, the default for non-waitable chains) and painting waits on that object before using the direct queue, so a driver-forced V-Sync can't make Present block the queue the asynchronous submission thread (0080) executes on (measured there: 44.5 -> 61.8 fps under forced V-Sync). Cvars d3d12_present_latency_wait (default true) and d3d12_present_test_sync_interval (testing).

The sync interval for testing is read just before Present (in the reference it sits a few lines earlier, where it is out of scope in this version of PaintAndPresentImpl).

